  "worked_solution": "First, we add a column for $P∨Q:$ \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨Q\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nNow, we add a column for $Q⇒(P∨Q).$ This statement is true unless $Q$ is true and $P∨Q$ is false. \n\n| $\\,P\\,$ | $\\,Q\\,$ | $\\,P∨Q\\,$ | $\\,Q⇒(P∨Q)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |",
